<< /A << /BBox [ 69.4488 100.63 525.373 380.466 ] /O /Layout >> /Alt (Six normalized confusion matrices show Clinical-BigBird performance across MIMIC-III and MIMIC-IV in-domain, zero-shot, and adaptation settings. Rows represent true labels and columns represent predicted labels for BEFORE, AFTER, OVERLAP, and NONE. The matrices show strong diagonal concentration overall, particularly for NONE, BEFORE, and OVERLAP. AFTER exhibits lower diagonal values and greater confusion with BEFORE, especially in zero-shot transfer. Adaptation generally strengthens diagonal performance relative to the corresponding zero-shot settings. Darker blue cells indicate larger normalized proportions, with color bars showing normalized values.) /K 2 /Lang (en-EN) /P 22 0 R /Pg 253 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
